framework Review:
  requires problem and premise and evidence and decision
  warns pending

problem P:
  |
    Make the shared focused authoring execution real rather than leave pure
    components whose only callers are tests. Preserve the accepted cc304 outcome.
premise AUTH:
  |
    After disclosure that common execution and the character adapter remain
    incomplete, the owner instructed correction. This authorizes local common
    runtime and consumer implementation, not paid calls or production activation.
evidence CODE:
  |
    The common orchestration has start select apply and finalize, and durable
    repositories have claimed runs reservation settlement and terminal records.
    No non-test caller currently drives them. Existing worker calls legacy V2.
    Character adapter omits revision text and has placeholder question behavior.
evidence CONTRACT:
  |
    Accepted ADR0031 and design revision2 require a generic typed kernel, effect
    ports, frozen source, scoped requests, cumulative limits, owner fences,
    source-based retries, final reconciliation and separate owner acceptance.
    The accepted new policy allows eight calls and USD0.50 per attempt. Current
    production behavior and shared Stage infrastructure remain unchanged.
pending LIMITS:
  |
    Actual model convergence and owner acceptance are not established locally.
    Completion of all API UI and migration obligations may span work sessions;
    no component completion or test pass can close cc304 on its own.
decision IMPLEMENT based_on P, AUTH, CODE, CONTRACT, LIMITS:
  |
    Implement the actual asynchronous shared execution driver with HTTP provider
    transport and durable reservation/terminal handling, consumed by a character
    application service and queued worker rather than test-only composition.
    Correct the new adapter's missing source/recovery behavior along that path.
    Keep the old V2 WIP untouched and do not switch production policy. Verify
    actual consumer execution with controlled local HTTP and database readback,
    including invalid output recovery and terminal replay with no extra calls.
    Prefer this to another legacy parser patch or an additional review control.
    Keep cc304 incomplete until all three owner-facing paths meet its criteria.

evidence RECOVERY_STATE:
  |
    orchestration decode rejection inserts issues.proposalRejected into findings.
    A subsequent valid proposal passes existing findings into stageProposal.
    The character adapter returns those findings unchanged from staging and
    reconciliation, and finalization rejects any remaining finding.
decision RECOVERY_FIX based_on RECOVERY_STATE, CONTRACT, IMPLEMENT:
  |
    The transient decoder finding is retained after its condition is gone on
    this path. Resolve only the kernel-owned proposal decode issue after a valid
    accepted transaction, not domain semantic findings. Verify with malformed
    then valid HTTP proposals traversing the same runtime and durable storage.
    This is a local recovery mechanism, not an RCA of earlier agent behavior.

evidence RUNTIME_INPUT:
  |
    The context projector supplies operation names without operation value schemas.
    The HTTP driver discards provider usage and settles every response as 1500
    output tokens; cumulative output policy is 8000. Resource guards reject equality
    after delivery, including the eighth admitted response. Registration does not
    compare source mode or frozen definition to the parent command and generation.
decision RUNTIME_CORRECTION based_on RUNTIME_INPUT, CONTRACT, IMPLEMENT:
  |
    Supply only active operation contracts, decode optional provider usage bounded
    by its reservation, and retain full reservation when usage is absent or invalid.
    Permit applying an already admitted response at the call or token ceiling;
    new admission still rejects a request that exceeds policy. Keep wall and step
    limits. Bind source kind and source generation to the queued owner command.
    These remove observed runtime mismatches; actual model quality remains unknown.

evidence SERIALIZATION:
  |
    The focused speech request contains 1041 operation-contract bytes, 2000 shared
    schema-definition bytes and 752 candidate bytes. Counting the HTTP JSON body
    again includes escaped quotes around the already serialized context, yielding
    7316 reserved tokens. The provider receives system and user message contents
    rather than those wire escaping characters as model input.
decision MESSAGE_BOUND based_on SERIALIZATION, CONTRACT, RUNTIME_CORRECTION:
  |
    Retain the one-token-per-UTF8-byte bound on system and user message contents
    plus the framing allowance. Continue bounding the entire HTTP body separately
    with maxInputBytesPerCall. Compress repeated prompt guidance without removing
    operation contracts. Do not lower the policy limits or assume four bytes/token.

evidence TERMINAL_INPUT:
  |
    The new worker binding validates source and current pointer before claiming
    the common run. Exceptions there are caught by the legacy worker, marking
    the parent failed but leaving the common run pending. Source retry requires
    a failed common run and therefore cannot resume such a parent.
decision TERMINAL_CORRECTION based_on TERMINAL_INPUT, CONTRACT, IMPLEMENT:
  |
    Claim first and persist a typed pre-dispatch failure in the same common and
    family terminal transaction for invalid source, pointer drift or unavailable
    provider. Keep all usage zero when no dispatch occurred. Do not retry errors
    or move the source pointer. This fixes lifecycle inconsistency, not detection.

evidence LEDGER_FLOW:
  |
    stageLedgerProposal creates a new sourceDispositions map for each proposal.
    Its input has no prior disposition map. Orchestration assigns that returned
    map to nextDispositions instead of merging prior entries. adapterView returns
    only candidate obligations and findings. Terminal identity omits the ledgers,
    while family storage receives only the terminal result.
decision RETAIN_LEDGER based_on LEDGER_FLOW, CONTRACT, IMPLEMENT:
  |
    Merge successfully staged disposition deltas into the prior ledger. Supply
    the provenance and disposition ledgers to adapter reconciliation/finalization
    views and retain their serializable entries in terminal results. Existing
    in-memory map values remain model proposals, not proof of source meaning.
    This corrects replacement and omission of recorded data, without claiming
    semantic validation or implementing a new character meaning contract.
